.TH EVERY 1 "September 2026" "every" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
every \- humane task scheduler for macOS (launchd), Linux (systemd), and Windows (Task Scheduler)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B every
.I schedule
.RB [ \-\-name
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-quiet ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.B \-\-
.I command\ ...
.br
.B every
.BR list " [" \-\-json ]
.br
.B every
.BR log | run | pause | resume | rm
.I name
.br
.B every
.BR doctor | version | help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B every
schedules a command with one human phrase and, unlike raw cron or launchd,
records every run so you can see whether it actually happened. It generates a
launchd agent (macOS), a systemd user timer (Linux), or a Windows Task
Scheduler task per task; the command runs through the platform shell in the
directory it was added from, and its output is captured to a per\-task log.
.SH SCHEDULE
.TP
.BI Ns " / " Nm " / " Nh
fixed interval (minimum 10s on Unix; 1m on Windows), e.g.\& \fB90s\fR, \fB15m\fR, \fB2h\fR
.TP
.B hourly
every hour
.TP
.BI "day " TIME
daily, e.g.\& \fBday 9am\fR, \fBday 17:30\fR, \fBday 9am,6pm\fR
.TP
.BI "weekdays " TIME " / " "weekends " TIME
Mon\-Fri / Sat+Sun
.TP
.IR WEEKDAY " " TIME
weekly, e.g.\& \fBmonday 10:00\fR, \fBmonday,thursday 6pm\fR
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B every \fIschedule\fR \-\- \fIcommand\fR
Schedule a task. The command is a shell command line (quote args with spaces
or metacharacters as at a prompt). Output goes to the log, not your terminal.
.TP
.B every list \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show every task: schedule, last run, status (ok / FAIL / unscheduled / paused),
next run. With \fB\-\-json\fR, emit one JSON object per task on stdout.
.TP
.B every log \fIname\fR \fR[\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR]
Print the last \fIN\fR (default 40) lines of a task's run log.
.TP
.B every run \fIname\fR
Run a task now, in your terminal \(em to test it before trusting the schedule.
.TP
.B every pause \fIname\fR \fR/\fB resume \fIname\fR
Stop / restart scheduling without deleting the task.
.TP
.B every rm \fIname\fR
Remove a task and its agent (the log is kept).
.TP
.B every doctor
Explain, in plain language, why a task isn't running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Name the task explicitly (otherwise it's derived from the command).
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Don't post a desktop notification when this task fails.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Kill a run (and its process group) that overruns, e.g.\& \fB\-\-timeout 30m\fR.
.TP
.BI \-n " N"
For \fBlog\fR: number of lines to show.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 64
usage error (bad arguments)
.TP
.B 66
no such task, or no logs yet
.TP
.B 1
other failure
.PP
.B every run
(and scheduled runs) exit with the command's own code, or
.B 124
on \fB\-\-timeout\fR, or
.B 128+signum
if a signal killed it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EVERY_HOME
Override the data directory entirely.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Data lives in \fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/every\fR (default \fB~/.local/share/every\fR).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
systemd user units on Linux (default \fB~/.config/systemd/user\fR).
.TP
.B LOCALAPPDATA
Native Windows data defaults to \fB%LOCALAPPDATA%\\every\fR.
.TP
.B EVERY_SHELL
Select the Windows shell executable (defaults to \fB%COMSPEC%\fR / cmd.exe).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI color (see https://no-color.org).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/every/tasks.json
task registry
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/every/logs/\fIname\fB.log
per\-task run output
.TP
.B ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.every.\fIname\fB.plist
launchd agent (macOS)
.TP
.B %LOCALAPPDATA%\\every
task registry and logs (native Windows)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
every day 9am \-\- brew update
every 15m \-\- ~/bin/sync\-notes.sh
every weekdays 9:30 \-\- ~/bin/standup\-prep.sh
every list \-\-json | jq \-r '.[] | select(.status | test("FAIL")) | .name'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR launchctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR schtasks (1),
.BR crontab (5)
.PP
Homepage: https://github.com/serhiileniv/every
